    "notes": "The land of High Peaks, MSM's own recipe rather than a copy of a vanilla file: rugged mountains up to about height 240. The noise router's final_density (msm_starter:high_peaks/final_density) shapes the land and its temperature picks the biomes. Above height 150 the ground is snow. The surface rule (material_rule) puts bedrock at the bottom, then grass over dirt on land, sand over sandstone in deserts and on beaches, sand under water, and stone everywhere else."
